# Copy to /etc/ducktape/coordinator.env and edit the one line below.
# This is NOT a secret — the coordinator holds no keys. It is only the bind addr.
#
# The wildcard bind is fully functional on a single-IP host (STUN + rendezvous
# + hole-punch all derive from the datagram's observed source). On a MULTI-HOMED
# host, bind the concrete public IP peers dial: replies from a wildcard socket
# egress with the route-chosen source IP, and clients discard replies that do
# not come from the address they dialed.
COORDINATOR_LISTEN=0.0.0.0:3478
# COORDINATOR_LISTEN=203.0.113.10:3478   # multi-homed: bind the dialed IP

# Runtime and optional auth arguments. The supplied value binds the TCP relay
# lane on 443 (the unit grants CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE for exactly this), enables
# four auth workers under the default public proof-of-possession policy, and
# emits a metrics row every 10 s. Keep the relay ON: every joiner derives its
# first-contact fallback as <this host>:443 and never learns otherwise. For
# private mode, point at the PUBLIC network descriptor; this is still not a
# secret.
COORDINATOR_ARGS=--relay-listen 0.0.0.0:443 --workers 4 --metrics-interval 10
# Behind a reverse proxy / NAT that forwards 443 to an unprivileged port:
# COORDINATOR_ARGS=--relay-listen 0.0.0.0:8443 --workers 4 --metrics-interval 10
# Deliberately no relay (joiners behind a non-punching NAT cannot join through here):
# COORDINATOR_ARGS=--relay-listen none --workers 4 --metrics-interval 10
# Private mode, following the validator set of a node on this host (drop
# --valset-node to admit against the genesis set alone):
# COORDINATOR_ARGS=--relay-listen 0.0.0.0:443 --workers 4 --metrics-interval 10 --genesis-set /etc/ducktape/network.toml --valset-node http://127.0.0.1:8844
